From 4fbd41fa2d50cceb6291a1c7f951a43dd9fcce7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:53:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(remote): client closes idle keep-alive sockets first;
 backend idle close 5 s -> 120 s

Desktop <-> hermes-hub flapped all night (53 "marked down (socket hang up)" in 03:00-04:23 PST, ~200
fail-fast lines per 10 min) on build fedc433cef. tcpdump of the hub proxy :9147: 197 requests in 7 min
were written into connections the backend had already closed, each closed after exactly 5.0 s idle
(uvicorn's default timeout_keep_alive). The FIN crosses the SSH tunnel only after Desktop has picked that
pooled socket for its next poll; Desktop's agents kept idle sockets forever. One such hang up marks the
whole remote down in remote-down-gate.

- hermes_cli: every uvicorn listener (web_server._build_uvicorn_server, build_listener_server) uses
  KEEP_ALIVE_IDLE_S = 120.
- Desktop: all pooled agents (json, probe, download) come from keepAliveAgent(), which closes a free
  socket after CLIENT_KEEPALIVE_IDLE_MS = 30 s, so the client always closes first.

Tests: keepalive-race.test.ts reproduces the race live (uvicorn-like server + FIN-delaying relay): the old
agent hangs up, keepAliveAgent never does; pins every pool to the idle timeout and its margin under the
server constant. test_web_server_ws_ping.py pins timeout_keep_alive on both listeners (fail on base).

Card: t_01a1d48ad4870953
